# Allowlist: the image gets only what the app needs to run. Everything else (docs, tests, git
# history, local settings such as .env, virtualenvs, editor/agent state such as ijfw/ and .ijfw/,
# deploy tooling, build scripts) stays out, including on local builds from a working copy.
*

!app/
!migrations/
!requirements/
!alembic.ini
!config.py
!gunicorn.conf.py
!run.py
!LICENSE
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md

# Container entrypoint and the Python maintenance scripts run with `docker exec`.
!scripts/docker_entrypoint.sh
!scripts/*.py

# Optional local copy of the embedding model (the build downloads it when absent).
!.hf-models/

# Never ship caches or local state, even inside the allowed folders.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.log
**/*.local
**/.env
